A subsystem of D induces a filter of the system of finitely generated subsystems. The filter confirms a neighbourhood exactly when that neighbourhood is the neighbourhood generated by a list whose basic neighbourhoods all lie in the subsystem. Such a witness is a neighbourhood of the system. The empty list witnesses the master neighbourhood, since it has no indices. The intersection of two confirmed neighbourhoods is the neighbourhood generated by the concatenation of their lists. If a confirmed neighbourhood lies above another neighbourhood of the system, the finitely generated family of the lower list is contained in that of the upper list, so the generator-wise criterion puts every basic neighbourhood of the lower list in the subsystem.
